A select group of History students took part in a VR workshop from Testimony 360, looking at the Holocaust and hearing the testimonies of survivors. Through the VR headsets, students were able to look around locations used during the Holocaust, and gain a greater understanding of the atrocities that took place. 🥽 Was this a glimpse into the future of teaching? 📷 Mr Sleeth
@harrispurley • Mar 25
Last week, our Year 9 scholars did greatly delight in a modern rendering of Shakespeare’s famed Romeo and Juliet at the Globe Theatre, that very house where once his plays were first brought to life. There was dancing most lively, swift-riding upon BMXs, and even the snatching of a phone. Verily, we were in London indeed.
@harrispurley • Mar 19
Year 12 & 13 Religious Studies students took their thinking to the next level at the Candle Conference with renowned philosopher Peter Vardy. From revisiting key topics to sharpening their argument skills, the day was all about exam readiness, critical thinking, and confidence. Future thinkers in the making—ready to question, challenge, and succeed. 🕯
We invite you to come along and see our academy for yourself with a personal tour.
